---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DATA_YEAR } from '../lib/salary';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms of use for SalaryByCity: informational-purpose data, no warranties, acceptable use, intellectual property, and liability limits — in plain English."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Effective date: January 1, {DATA_YEAR}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      Welcome to SalaryByCity. By accessing or using this website, you agree to these terms. We've
      written them in plain English because terms nobody can read protect nobody. If you do not
      agree with them, please do not use the site.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">1. What this site is — and isn't</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      SalaryByCity publishes salary statistics and related context (cost of living, taxes,
      employment patterns) <strong>for general informational purposes only</strong>. Our figures are
      statistical estimates derived from public government data as described on our
      <a href="/methodology/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">methodology page</a>.
      They are not an offer of employment, a promise of pay, or financial, legal, tax, or career
      advice. Salary decisions — accepting an offer, negotiating, relocating — should account for
      your individual circumstances, and where the stakes are high, a qualified professional.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">2. Accuracy and availability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      We work hard to keep the data current and correct, and we document our update schedule
      publicly. Even so, the site is provided <strong>"as is" and "as available," without warranties
      of any kind</strong>, express or implied — including accuracy, completeness, merchantability,
      or fitness for a particular purpose. Government source data is revised, suppressed, and
      re-benchmarked over time; labor markets move between our updates. We may modify, suspend, or
      discontinue any part of the site at any time without notice.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">3. Acceptable use and intellectual property</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      You may use, quote, and share our pages for personal, educational, journalistic, and internal
      business purposes, with attribution and (online) a link back. You may not scrape or
      republish the site wholesale, misrepresent our estimates as official BLS publications, use the
      site to build a competing dataset by systematic extraction, or attempt to disrupt its
      operation. The underlying government statistics are public domain; our original text,
      calculations, design, and code are ours, and all rights not expressly granted are reserved.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">4. Third-party links and advertising</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      Pages link to external resources (such as bls.gov) and display third-party advertising. We do
      not control and are not responsible for external sites or advertised products. The presence of
      an advertisement is not an endorsement. Our <a href="/privacy/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">Privacy Policy</a>
      explains how advertising cookies work here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">5. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, SalaryByCity and its operators will not be liable for
      any indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages — including lost profits, lost
      opportunities, or employment decisions — arising from your use of, or inability to use, this
      site or its data. Your sole and exclusive remedy for dissatisfaction with the site is to stop
      using it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">6. Changes and contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      We may update these terms from time to time; the effective date above always reflects the
      current version, and continued use after a change constitutes acceptance. Questions about
      these terms are welcome at
      <a href="mailto:legal@salarybycity.com" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">legal@salarybycity.com</a>
      or via our <a href="/contact/" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
